, 15 . Implying something surprising or unexpected, even, indeed Job 14:3 ; 15:4 *. וְאַף and also Lev 26:39-40 , 42 , 44 ; Deut 15:17 ; Hab 2:15 ; Psa 68:19 ; 1Chr 8:32 * = 9:38 * 2Chr 12:5 * Neh 2:18 ; 13:15 ; and even Job 19:4 שָׁגִיתִי וְאַףאָֿמְנָם and even indeed (if) I have erred . . . With הַאַף הֲ, indeed . . .. really . . .. Gen 18:13 , 23 wilt thou indeed sweep away the righteous with the wicked? 18:24 ; Amos 2:11 ; Job 34:17 ; 40:8 . In contrast to a preceding thought (expressed or implied) but, nay ( imo ) Psa 44:10 ; 58:3 ; compare Judg 5:29 *. 2 (Equally in prose and poetry) with reference to a preceding sentence, yea, à fortiori, the more so (= how much more! after an affirm. clause; = how much less! after a negative one): 2Sam 4:10 f. when one told me, Saul is dead . . . I took hold of him and slew him . . . וג הָרְגוּ רְשָׁעִים כִּיאֲֿנָשִׁים ׳אַף à fortiori, how much more (should I do so when wicked men have slain a righteous person, etc.! Ezek 14:21 (Ew Hi) 15:5 ; Prov 21:27 (in all these passages כִּי = when ) Job 4:19 . So וְאַף 1Sam 23:3 ; 2Kin 5:13 . . . אֵלֶיךָ כִּיאָֿמַר וְאַף and the more (= and how much rather ), when he hath said to thee, etc. More commonly in this sense strengthened by כִּי (q. v.), see below כִּי אַף 1 furthermore Ezek 23:40 ; Hab 2:5 (Ges quin imo, quin etiam ). 2 in a question, indeed (is it) that . . .. Gen 3:1 אֱלֹהִים כִּיאָֿמַר אַף indeed, that God has said . . .. i.e. has God really said . . .. (compare הַאַף above). 3 with reference to a preceding sentence (which is often introduced by הֵן or הִנֵּה ), yea, that . . .! i.e. how much more (or less ) ! Prov 11:31 lo, the righteous is recompensed in the earth וְחוֺטֵא רָשָׁע כִּי ַאֹף 'tis indeed that (= how much more) the wicked and the sinner! 15:11 ; 17:7 ; 19:7 , 10 ; Job 9:14 ; 15:16 ; 25:6 ; 1Sam 14:30 ; 1Kin 8:27 (= 2Chr 6:18 ) lo, the heavens . . . cannot contain thee הַזֶּה הַבַּיִת כִּי אַ֕ף 'tis indeed that this house (cannot do so), i.e. how much less this house! 32:15 . So כִּי וְאַף Deut 31:27 ; 1Sam 21:6 (perhaps; but see RS Semitic i. 436 Dr Sm 293 ) 2Sam 16:11 . (In Job 35:14 (Hi De) Neh 9:18 כִּי אַף is simply = yea, when . . .) אפד (existence & meaning dubious Thes MV and others identify with אָפַד gird on , but this denominative see below; Lag BN 178; GN 1890, p. 15 proposes , come as ambassador , as √ of אֵפוֺר ). אַף conjunction also (Biblical Hebrew אַף ; Egyptian Aramaic, Palmyrene אף (S-C Pap. Lzb 224 ); ᵑ7 אַף, ᵑ7 J also אוֺף ; Syriac ; — also , alwlays וְאַף Dan 6:23 ; Ezra 5:10 , 14 ; 6:5 .","rootNote":"a primitive particle;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 8 32","keyReferences":["1Chr 8 32","1Chr 9 38","1Chr 16 30","1Kgs 8 27","1Sam 2 7","1Sam 14 30","1Sam 21 6","1Sam 23 3"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":134,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 8 32","book":"1Chr","chapter":8,"verse":32,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אַף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/D"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 38","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":38,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אַף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/D"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 30","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 8 27","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֕ף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 7","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 30","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֗ף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 21 6","book":"1Sam","chapter":21,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אַ֕ף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/D"},{"reference":"1Sam 23 3","book":"1Sam","chapter":23,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אַף֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/D"},{"refe